            <ArticleTitle>Coronary stents: current status.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S1-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jacc.2010.06.007</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery stents revolutionized the practice of interventional cardiology after they were first introduced in the mid-1980s. Since then, there have been significant developments in their design, the most notable of which has been the introduction of drug-eluting stents. This paper reviews the benefits, risks, and current status of Food and Drug Administration-approved drug-eluting stents.</AbstractText>
